spec:R9.19 a specl:Requirement ;
    specl:partOf <https://zwelz3.github.io/holonic/spec.ttl> ;
    dct:title "The library MUST ship a JupyterLite static build of the example notebooks for…" ;
    dct:description "The library MUST ship a JupyterLite static build of the example notebooks for in-browser exploration without local Python installation. Build integrates with the existing `notebooks/` directory via `scripts/sync_notebooks_to_jlite.py`; output lands in `docs/source/_extra/jupyterlite/` so Sphinx's `html_extra_path` serves it at `/jupyterlite/` alongside the documentation. Notebook 13 (yFiles visualization) is excluded from in-browser execution because yFiles requires a Jupyter server extension that Pyodide cannot provide; the landing notebook `00_start_here.ipynb` documents this constraint." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom spec:source-dcc526b3 ;
    specl:sourceLine "493"^^xsd:integer ;
    specl:priority "MUST" ;
    specl:implementationStatus "verified" ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-f0c9c1bd ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-c8bff8ac ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-8b28ba38 ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-9bec9ac2 ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-4b557245 ;
    specl:acceptanceCriterion "Given the hosted documentation, when a reader opens the docs and follows the \"Try in browser\" link, then the JupyterLite lab loads and notebooks 01-12 execute against a Pyodide kernel without local Python installation." ;
    specl:verifiedBy spec:test-b8307716 .

spec:R9.20 a specl:Requirement ;
    specl:partOf <https://zwelz3.github.io/holonic/spec.ttl> ;
    dct:title "The library MUST provide `HolonicDataset.remove_holon(iri)` completing the CRUD…" ;
    dct:description "The library MUST provide `HolonicDataset.remove_holon(iri)` completing the CRUD lifecycle started by `add_holon()`. Cleans up the holon's registry entry, all four layer graphs (interior/boundary/projection/context), graph-typing triples, graph-level metadata records, the per-holon rollup, and cascades to `remove_portal()` for every portal where the holon is source or target. Child holons that reference the removed holon via `cga:memberOf` are orphaned (their `memberOf` triple is removed) but not themselves deleted. Idempotent — returns `False` for a non-existent IRI rather than raising. Provenance activities referencing the removed holon are preserved because provenance is immutable history." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom spec:source-dcc526b3 ;
    specl:sourceLine "502"^^xsd:integer ;
    specl:priority "MUST" ;
    specl:implementationStatus "verified" ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-c8573464 ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-bb929637 ;
    specl:acceptanceCriterion "Given a holon with interior, boundary, and context layer graphs, plus a portal from it and a portal to it, plus a child holon referencing it as `cga:memberOf`, when `remove_holon(iri)` is called, then the holon is gone from `list_holons()`, all four layer graphs are deleted via `backend.graph_exists()=False`, both portals are gone from `find_portals_from`/`find_portals_to`, and the child remains in `list_holons()` but without its `memberOf` triple." ;
    specl:verifiedBy spec:test-7e231872 .

spec:R9.21 a specl:Requirement ;
    specl:partOf <https://zwelz3.github.io/holonic/spec.ttl> ;
    dct:title "The library MUST provide `HolonicDataset.remove_portal(portal_iri)` completing…" ;
    dct:description "The library MUST provide `HolonicDataset.remove_portal(portal_iri)` completing the CRUD lifecycle started by `add_portal()`. Removes all triples with `portal_iri` as subject from every graph containing them (typically the source holon's boundary graph and the registry mirror). The boundary graph itself is preserved — sibling portals and SHACL shapes in the same graph are unaffected. Idempotent — returns `False` for a non-existent portal IRI rather than raising. Metadata refresh fires per affected graph when `metadata_updates=\"eager\"`." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom spec:source-dcc526b3 ;
    specl:sourceLine "509"^^xsd:integer ;
    specl:priority "MUST" ;
    specl:implementationStatus "verified" ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-61d6e316 ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-bb929637 ;
    specl:acceptanceCriterion "Given a source holon with two portals declared in the same boundary graph plus a SHACL shape, when `remove_portal(portal_a)` is called, then portal_a is absent from `find_portals_from(source)`, portal_b is still discoverable, and the SHACL shape is still present in the boundary graph." ;
    specl:verifiedBy spec:test-79c15c62 .

spec:R9.22 a specl:Requirement ;
    specl:partOf <https://zwelz3.github.io/holonic/spec.ttl> ;
    dct:title "The `add_portal()` method MUST support creation of all portal subtypes declared…" ;
    dct:description "The `add_portal()` method MUST support creation of all portal subtypes declared in the CGA ontology (`cga:TransformPortal`, `cga:IconPortal`, `cga:SealedPortal`) as well as downstream subclasses via three additive parameters: `construct_query` is optional (default `None`); `portal_type` is a customizable RDF type (default `\"cga:TransformPortal\"`); `extra_ttl` accepts additional Turtle triples for predicates carried by downstream portal subclasses. All existing positional calls continue to work unchanged. Portal discovery (`find_portals_from/to/direct`) MUST match any portal subtype — the pre-0.4.2 hardcoded filter on `cga:TransformPortal` is relaxed because the `cga:sourceHolon` + `cga:targetHolon` predicate pair uniquely identifies a portal regardless of its specific subtype. Discovery queries use `SELECT DISTINCT` to deduplicate results across the boundary graph and registry mirror. The CGA ontology ships `cga:IconPortal` (previously undeclared) and SHACL shapes (`cga:IconPortalShape`, `cga:SealedPortalShape`) that warn when these subtypes carry `cga:constructQuery`; `cga:TransformPortalShape` continues to require exactly one `cga:constructQuery`." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom spec:source-dcc526b3 ;
    specl:sourceLine "516"^^xsd:integer ;
    specl:priority "MUST" ;
    specl:implementationStatus "verified" ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-b0376446 ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-bb929637 ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-0f0766c7 ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-FIND_PORTALS_TO ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-707cae84 ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-d76cde6b ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-7540ee22 ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-c6777c34 ;
    specl:acceptanceCriterion "Given a portal created with `portal_type=\"cga:SealedPortal\"` and no `construct_query`, when `find_portals_from(source)` is called, then exactly one `PortalInfo` is returned with `construct_query=None`; and given a portal created with `extra_ttl` carrying a downstream predicate, when the boundary graph is queried by SPARQL for that predicate, then the extra triples are present; and given a TransformPortal without a constructQuery or a SealedPortal/IconPortal carrying one, when the registry is validated against `cga-shapes.ttl`, then the corresponding shape reports a violation (for TransformPortal) or warning (for SealedPortal and IconPortal)." ;
    specl:verifiedBy spec:test-ca8975b8 .

spec:R9.23 a specl:Requirement ;
    specl:partOf <https://zwelz3.github.io/holonic/spec.ttl> ;
    dct:title "Portal discovery queries MUST return the portal's RDF type (excluding base…" ;
    dct:description "Portal discovery queries MUST return the portal's RDF type (excluding base `cga:Portal`) as a `portal_type` field on `PortalInfo`, `PortalSummary`, and `PortalDetail`. All five discovery SPARQL queries include `OPTIONAL { ?portal a ?portalType . FILTER(?portalType != cga:Portal) }`." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom spec:source-dcc526b3 ;
    specl:sourceLine "525"^^xsd:integer ;
    specl:priority "MUST" ;
    specl:implementationStatus "verified" ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-8cc28144 ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-f8bc0c2d ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-157a532e ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-d6622f19 ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-bb929637 ;
    specl:acceptanceCriterion "Given a TransformPortal, when `find_portals_from()` is called, then `portal.portal_type` contains `\"urn:holonic:ontology:TransformPortal\"`. Given a SealedPortal, when `get_portal()` is called, then `detail.portal_type` contains `\"SealedPortal\"`." ;
    specl:verifiedBy spec:test-eed9ab82 .

spec:R9.24 a specl:Requirement ;
    specl:partOf <https://zwelz3.github.io/holonic/spec.ttl> ;
    dct:title "`traverse_portal()` MUST check the portal's RDF type before executing the…" ;
    dct:description "`traverse_portal()` MUST check the portal's RDF type before executing the CONSTRUCT query. If the portal is `cga:SealedPortal`, it MUST raise `SealedPortalError` (a `ValueError` subclass) regardless of whether the portal carries a `constructQuery`." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom spec:source-dcc526b3 ;
    specl:sourceLine "532"^^xsd:integer ;
    specl:priority "MUST" ;
    specl:implementationStatus "verified" ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-ec19ae50 ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-aa42bdec ;
    specl:acceptanceCriterion "Given a SealedPortal with or without a CONSTRUCT query, when `traverse_portal()` or `traverse()` is called, then `SealedPortalError` is raised with a message identifying the portal." ;
    specl:verifiedBy spec:test-48cd2f59 .

spec:R9.25 a specl:Requirement ;
    specl:partOf <https://zwelz3.github.io/holonic/spec.ttl> ;
    dct:title "`traverse()` MUST register the target interior graph as `cga:hasInterior` after…" ;
    dct:description "`traverse()` MUST register the target interior graph as `cga:hasInterior` after injection. It MUST look up existing registered interiors first and inject into the first one found; if none exist, it falls back to the `{target_iri}/interior` convention name. This ensures `validate_membrane()` can see the injected data." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom spec:source-dcc526b3 ;
    specl:sourceLine "539"^^xsd:integer ;
    specl:priority "MUST" ;
    specl:implementationStatus "verified" ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-040f5fe0 ;
    specl:acceptanceCriterion "Given a target holon with no pre-existing interior, when `traverse()` injects triples, then `GET_HOLON_INTERIORS` returns the injected graph and `validate_membrane()` validates against the injected data, not an empty graph." ;
    specl:verifiedBy spec:test-a1a4925b .

spec:R9.26 a specl:Requirement ;
    specl:partOf <https://zwelz3.github.io/holonic/spec.ttl> ;
    dct:title "`get_holon()` MUST use a direct filtered SPARQL query (O(1) in holarchy size)…" ;
    dct:description "`get_holon()` MUST use a direct filtered SPARQL query (O(1) in holarchy size) rather than scanning all holons via `iter_holons()`." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom spec:source-dcc526b3 ;
    specl:sourceLine "546"^^xsd:integer ;
    specl:priority "MUST" ;
    specl:implementationStatus "verified" ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-4a33892f ;
    specl:acceptanceCriterion "Given 20 holons, when `get_holon()` is called, then the method source does not reference `iter_holons`." ;
    specl:verifiedBy spec:test-e23c4b01 .

spec:R9.27 a specl:Requirement ;
    specl:partOf <https://zwelz3.github.io/holonic/spec.ttl> ;
    dct:title "`validate_all()` MUST validate membranes for all holons and return `dict[str…" ;
    dct:description "`validate_all()` MUST validate membranes for all holons and return `dict[str, MembraneResult]`." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom spec:source-dcc526b3 ;
    specl:sourceLine "553"^^xsd:integer ;
    specl:priority "MUST" ;
    specl:implementationStatus "verified" ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-427abfc7 ;
    specl:acceptanceCriterion "Given 2 holons, when `validate_all()` is called, then a dict with 2 entries is returned, each value a `MembraneResult`." ;
    specl:verifiedBy spec:test-521eea57 .

spec:R9.28 a specl:Requirement ;
    specl:partOf <https://zwelz3.github.io/holonic/spec.ttl> ;
    dct:title "`traverse()` MUST accept `fail_on_breach: bool = False`" ;
    dct:description "`traverse()` MUST accept `fail_on_breach: bool = False`. When True and validation returns COMPROMISED, it MUST roll back injected triples and raise `MembraneBreachError`. Rollback restores a pre-injection snapshot of the target interior." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom spec:source-dcc526b3 ;
    specl:sourceLine "560"^^xsd:integer ;
    specl:priority "MUST" ;
    specl:implementationStatus "verified" ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-040f5fe0 ;
    specl:acceptanceCriterion "Given a traversal that produces COMPROMISED validation, when `fail_on_breach=True`, then `MembraneBreachError` is raised and the target interior is unchanged. See OQ11 for the SHACL coverage gap." ;
    specl:verifiedBy spec:test-f9074661 .

spec:R9.29 a specl:Requirement ;
    specl:partOf <https://zwelz3.github.io/holonic/spec.ttl> ;
    dct:title "`update_portal()` MUST update portal properties in-place without requiring…" ;
    dct:description "`update_portal()` MUST update portal properties in-place without requiring remove+add. Uses per-graph SPARQL DELETE for old values and Turtle parse for new values." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom spec:source-dcc526b3 ;
    specl:sourceLine "567"^^xsd:integer ;
    specl:priority "MUST" ;
    specl:implementationStatus "verified" ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-7ce1c168 ;
    specl:acceptanceCriterion "Given a portal with a CONSTRUCT query, when `update_portal(construct_query=new_query)` is called, then `get_portal()` returns the new query." ;
    specl:verifiedBy spec:test-6e816b28 .

spec:R9.30 a specl:Requirement ;
    specl:partOf <https://zwelz3.github.io/holonic/spec.ttl> ;
    dct:title "`traverse_path()` MUST execute multi-hop traversals by calling `find_path()`…" ;
    dct:description "`traverse_path()` MUST execute multi-hop traversals by calling `find_path()` then looping `traverse()`. Raises `ValueError` if no path exists. Records provenance per hop when `agent_iri` is provided." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom spec:source-dcc526b3 ;
    specl:sourceLine "574"^^xsd:integer ;
    specl:priority "MUST" ;
    specl:implementationStatus "verified" ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-fba03f4f ;
    specl:acceptanceCriterion "Given a 3-holon chain A->B->C, when `traverse_path(\"A\", \"C\")` is called, then 2 hops are executed and provenance records exist for each." ;
    specl:verifiedBy spec:test-eb7952b6 .

spec:R9.31 a specl:Requirement ;
    specl:partOf <https://zwelz3.github.io/holonic/spec.ttl> ;
    dct:title "`dry_run()` MUST simulate a traversal without mutating state" ;
    dct:description "`dry_run()` MUST simulate a traversal without mutating state. Runs the CONSTRUCT, merges with existing interiors in memory, validates against boundary shapes, and returns `(projected_graph, membrane_result)`." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom spec:source-dcc526b3 ;
    specl:sourceLine "581"^^xsd:integer ;
    specl:priority "MUST" ;
    specl:implementationStatus "verified" ;
    specl:constrains spec:component-21773f6b ;
    specl:acceptanceCriterion "Given a source and target with data, when `dry_run()` is called, then projected triples are returned, a membrane result is returned, and the target interior is empty." ;
    specl:verifiedBy spec:test-2a22d069 .

spec:R9.32 a specl:Requirement ;
